Patch-ID: P-APP-001 (wave-5 slice 1) — ReArcAppDelegate and menu installation
at the PreCreateThreads seam.
Rationale: second milestone of engine/docs/patches/P-APP-001.md, patch-map row
"chrome_browser_main_mac.mm PreCreateThreads(): replace the
nil-delegate/AppController/BuildMainMenu/mainMenuCreated block with bridge
delegate/menu installation". When an engine lifecycle host is registered
(ReArcEngineSetLifecycleCallbacks, patch app/002), PreCreateThreads now
installs the retained ReArcAppDelegate plus the placeholder bridge menu via
rearc::InstallReArcAppDelegateAndMenu() and returns, so AppController is never
instantiated (its sharedController identity CHECK forbids a second delegate
owner). When no host is registered the gate is off and the stock
AppController/BuildMainMenu block runs bit-identically. The menu surface stays
the slice-1 placeholder (empty NSMenu titled "ReArc"); shell-owned menu
construction is a later slice. chrome::BuildMainMenu and app_controller_mac.h
remain referenced by the stock path; no includes are removed.
Gate: rearc::GetEngineLifecycleHost() != nullptr. Bit-identical stock behavior
with the gate off is the acceptance invariant; validated with Chromium
--version only (no interactive runs this wave).
Drift check @ 156.0.8078.74 (2026-11-01): none. The PreCreateThreads
nil-delegate/AppController/BuildMainMenu/mainMenuCreated block is at
chrome_browser_main_mac.mm:159-174 after this patch (was :151-166 pre-patch,
as recorded in the P-APP-001 drift log); InstallReArcAppDelegateAndMenu()
keeps the upstream CHECK_EQ(nil, NSApp.delegate) invariant.
Upstream hunks: chrome/browser/chrome_browser_main_mac.mm only (two rearc
includes + the gated installation block). No BUILD.gn change: patch 002
already wired the //chrome/browser/rearc_bridge dep into the is_mac block of
the target owning this file (chrome/browser/BUILD.gn:1553).
Last rebased: 2026-11-01 @ 156.0.8078.74.

